  "summary": "A soft starter reduces the starting current and torque shock of an AC motor. Anti-parallel thyristor (SCR) pairs in each phase let through only part of each half-cycle at first (reduced voltage); the firing angle is advanced over the ramp time until full voltage is reached, then a bypass contactor closes. Unlike a VFD, it does not change the running speed — only how the motor starts and stops.",
  "classification": {
    "family": "Power electronic motor starter",
    "type": "3-phase controlled soft starter with internal bypass"
  },
  "model_configuration": {
    "animation": "Motor accelerates smoothly during the ramp; bypass contacts close; motor then coasts to stop"
  },
